 'Project Init':{title:'Claude Mouse',format:'1920 × 1080 · 16:9',rate:'24 fps',direction:'A local film project with explicit source assignments.'},
 'Audio Analysis':{affect:'Unease → resolve → relief',pacing:'Build through the confrontation; release into the final street view.',direction:'The change at 12 seconds supports the engine awakening. Preserve the assigned song as the timing source.'},
 Brief:{premise:'A small mouse turns the cat’s tools of control into comfort for the town.',protagonist:'Claude Mouse',change:'From isolated fear to shared agency',protect:'The mouse makes the decisive choice. No rescue by an outside hero.',direction:'A clear, visual transformation. Let the town’s changing use of the street carry the ending.'},
 'Production Design':{look:'Miniature frontier town · stylized tactile materials',palette:'Warm ochre · aged brass · muted blue shadows',camera:'Repeat the low street master. Preserve the porch/street axis.',continuity:'The Comfort Engine stays on the street; wardrobe and brass cog remain consistent.',direction:'Light and occupancy change over time. Keep the architecture and character silhouettes stable.'},
 Treatment:{opening:'The empty street belongs to the cat. A mouse arrives carrying a brass cog.',conflict:'The cat blocks the porch. The mouse chooses the street mechanism instead of confrontation.',resolution:'The repaired engine provides comfort. The town returns; the cat loses its monopoly.',direction:'Because the porch is blocked, the mouse redirects its effort. The visible repair causes the town to return.'}
